From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:31:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/paddr: fix wrong report filtering address

It should do filtering for the probing memory.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 mm/damon/paddr.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/damon/paddr.c b/mm/damon/paddr.c
index 2774f3cf10a2b..f882011c695a2 100644
--- a/mm/damon/paddr.c
+++ b/mm/damon/paddr.c
@@ -224,10 +224,10 @@ static bool damon_pa_filter_match(struct damon_filter *filter,
 			matched = damon_folio_young(folio) == false;
 		break;
 	case DAMON_FILTER_TYPE_REPORT:
-		addr_range.start = filter->report_addr_start;
-		addr_range.end = filter->report_addr_end;
-		matched = damon_report_exist(filter->report_type,
-				&addr_range, jiffies -
+		addr_range.start = pa;
+		addr_range.end = pa + 1;
+		matched = damon_report_exist(filter->report_type, &addr_range,
+				jiffies -
 				usecs_to_jiffies(ctx->attrs.sample_interval));
 		break;
 	default:
-- 
2.47.3

